    "text": "Consider a sphere of radius <math><mi>R</mi></math> which carries a uniform charge density <math><mi>&#961;</mi></math> . If a sphere of radius <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> is carved out of it, as shown, the ratio <math><mfrac><mrow><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math> of magnitude of electric field <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> and <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> , respectively, at points <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math> due to the remaining portion is:<br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/1d906c2f-f6dd-46d1-bacc-ff9bafefef21-image.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 223px;\" />",
